; Output: MACRO.M
; Console: MACRO.OUT
; PMDMML.MAN §3-2, §16-1

#Title MACRO
#Option /v/c

; §16-1 Defined Variable Usage (!)
!Foo c d e              ; Define string variable Foo
!1 f g a                ; Define numeric variable 1
A !Foo !1 b             ; Use variables

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Named variables
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A named variable is declared by a line whose first character is '!'. The
; value is the rest of that line and is compiled wherever the variable is
; used, so it can hold any MML.

!V1 c d e
!V2 v12 l8 @1 o4
!V3 v6
!Len l4

; Used at the start of a line, in the middle, and at the end of one
A !V1
A !V2 !V1
A v3 c d !V1 g f
A g f e !V1
A v8 l8 !V1 !V1

; Values may contain loops, ties, rests and length changes
!Loop [ c d ]2
!Tie c4&c4
A !Len !Loop !Tie r
A v9 l8 [ !V1 !Tie ]2 r

; A variable may be used in the value of another variable
!Nest !V1 f g
A v4 !Nest a b >c

; Redeclaring a variable replaces its value from that point on
!Red c d
A v5 !Red
!Red e f
A v5 !Red

; Variables are usable from the rhythm part as well
!Drum \V63 \b l4
K !Drum \s \h \cp

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Numeric variables
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; '!' followed by a number declares and uses !0 through !255

!0 v10 l4
!1 c d e
!9 r r r
!16 e f g
!255 a b >c
A !0 !1 !255
A !$10 !9

; Leading zeros are ignored
!0000 v2 l2 c d e
A !0 f g

; The declared index is truncated to 8 bits, so !256 is the same as !0
!256 v13 l1
A v14 !0 c d e f

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Names are at most 30 characters long
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Thirty characters: VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ

; The name ends the line: the rest of the part must not bleed into the next
!VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ l8 c d
A v14 !VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ
A v3 f g a b >c d e f g

; Followed by another command on the same line
A v14 !VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ r r

; Longer names are truncated to their first 30 characters
!VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ_EXTRA v13 e f
A !VAR0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQ

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Prefix matching
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; A name that the used name starts with is accepted, and the rest of the used
; name is compiled as MML, so no space is needed after the variable

!Pfx c d
A v14 !Pfxl4 e f

; An exact match wins over a prefix match
!PfxLong g a b
A v14 !PfxLong !Pfx

; The longest prefix wins, whichever of the two is declared first
!A1B e f
!A1 c d
A v14 !A1Bl8 g
A v14 !A1l16 g

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Other parts and part-limited MML
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Ssg v10 l4
G !Ssg o5 c d
B !V1 !Ssg e

; A value may also end with another variable
!Inner2 c d
!Outer2 v14 f !Inner2
A !Outer2 g

; Variables are expanded after the part letters in a | group
AB| !V1 |!A !Pfx | e f

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Declarations are collected before the parts are compiled
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
A v7 !Late c d e

; Declared after all of its uses
!Late a b >c

; Named macro with prefix matching: define MyMacro, use prefix My
!MyMacro c d e
!MyOther f g a

; Use named macro (exact match)
A !MyMacro

; Use named macro prefix (prefix match - MyO matches MyOther)
A !MyOther

; Named macro definitions
!MyMacro c d e
!MyOther f g a

; Use named macros
A !MyMacro !MyOther b

; Named macro with prefix match
!LongMacroName c d e
!Long f g a

; Use exact match
A !LongMacroName
; Use prefix match (Long matches LongMacroName as prefix)
A !Long
